<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ============================================================
    ic_document — document/file glyph (attach menu, doc bubble)
    ===
    Referenced by:
      - bottom_sheet_attach.xml (option_document leading icon)
      - future: document message bubble type badge (Phase 7)
      - future: "open file" affordance in a document bubble

    Constraints this file honors:

    1. MONOCHROME TEMPLATE.
       Single fill color (#FFFFFFFF), tinted at the consumer
       level (app:tint="?attr/colorOnSurface" in
       bottom_sheet_attach.xml). Do NOT set a brand color
       here — the fill is a template.

    2. 24dp VIEWPORT.
       Matches every other chrome icon in the app. The attach
       sheet renders it at 24dp; the document-bubble badge
       will render it at 16dp in the corner of the file
       preview — the vector scales losslessly.

    3. STANDARD MATERIAL "DESCRIPTION" GLYPH.
       This is Google's canonical Material Design
       "description" icon: a document sheet with a folded
       corner at the top-right and three horizontal text
       lines in the body. It is NOT a custom design. Every
       file-management and messaging app uses essentially
       this shape for "document," and users recognize it
       instantly.

    4. FILLED SHAPE, OUTLINED INTERIOR (evenOdd).
       The document sheet is a solid filled shape with the
       folded corner and the three text lines punched out
       as transparent regions. This is the standard Material
       construction — the filled sheet reads as "a physical
       document," and the cutouts read as "content."

       Do NOT switch to the "description_outlined" variant
       (border-only document with solid text lines inside).
       That variant is appropriate for toolbar action icons
       where the icon must not compete with surrounding
       content. In the attach sheet, a filled icon has the
       right visual weight to indicate "tap to send a
       document" and matches the other four filled icons
       in the option row.

    5. SINGLE PATH WITH TWO CONTOURS, evenOdd.
       The path data contains:
         - Outer contour: the document sheet with the
           folded corner (a 6-sided polygon)
         - Inner contour: the three text lines + the
           folded corner cutout (a 7-sided shape formed
           by the three line rects and the fold triangle)

       Both contours are in a single <path> element with
       fillType="evenOdd", producing the correct cutouts
       regardless of winding direction. This is more robust
       than relying on opposite windings (which some
       tooling might normalize in the future) and produces
       a pixel-identical result to Google's reference.

    6. NO androidx.AutoMirrored.
       The document glyph is not directional — the folded
       corner is conventionally at the top-right regardless
       of text direction. Mirroring under RTL would
       produce a non-standard orientation that would look
       wrong to users. Do not add auto-mirroring.

    Rendering result at 24dp:
      A document sheet with a folded corner at the top-right
      and three horizontal text lines — instant recognition
      as "document / file."
    ============================================================
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">

    <!--
        Canonical Material Design "description" path data.

        Outer contour (document sheet with folded corner):
          M 14,2                     top-left of the sheet,
                                     just before the fold
          H 6                        right across the top edge
                                     to the fold's left edge
          c -1.1,0 -1.99,0.9 -1.99,2
                                     top-left corner curve
                                     (radius ~1.1 units)
          L 4,20                     left edge down to near
                                     the bottom
          c 0,1.1 0.9,2 2,2          bottom-left corner curve
          h 12                       right across the bottom
          c 1.1,0 2,-0.9 2,-2        bottom-right corner curve
          V 8                        up the right edge to
                                     where the fold meets
          h -4                       left into the fold's
                                     inner corner (4 units)
          V 2                        up to the top of the
                                     fold
          z                          close (implicit line
                                     from fold top back
                                     to start)

        Inner contour (folded corner + 3 text lines):
          M 16,6                     top-right of the folded
                                     corner (after the fold's
                                     inner step)
          v 2                        down 2 units (fold
                                     triangle height)
          H 8                        left to x=8
          V 9                        down 1 unit (top text
                                     line's top edge)
          h 8                        right to x=16
          V 11                       down 2 units (top text
                                     line's bottom edge
                                     and start of the gap
                                     before the next line)
          H 8                        left to x=8
          V 12                       down 1 unit (second
                                     text line's top edge)
          h 8                        right to x=16
          V 14                       down 2 units (second
                                     text line's bottom
                                     edge and gap)
          H 8                        left to x=8
          V 15                       down 1 unit (third
                                     text line's top edge)
          h 8                        right to x=16
          V 16                       down 2 units (third
                                     text line's bottom
                                     edge)
          H 8                        left to x=8
          z                          close

        Rendered under evenOdd, the sheet is filled and the
        folded corner cutout + three text-line gaps appear
        as transparent regions — producing the standard
        "document" appearance.
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M14,2H6c-1.1,0 -1.99,0.9 -1.99,2L4,20c0,1.1 0.9,2 2,2h12c1.1,0 2,-0.9 2,-2V8h-6V2zM16,18H8v-2h8v2zM16,14H8v-2h8v2zM16,10H8V8h8v2z" />

</vector>
